}}|subdivision_type1=|subdivision_name1=|area_km2=995,596.89|population_census=7,559,628|population_census_year=2025|regional_languages=|common_languages=[[Baliscano]], [[Burawi language|Burawi]], [[Mozbayani]] (also recognized)|cctld=.pda|government_type={{W|Liquid democracy}}|ethnic_groups={{vunblist |item_style=white-space:nowrap;  |61.2% [[Baliscans]]<br> 38.8% Others}}|ethnic_groups_year=2023|motto={{vunblist |{{native phrase|tpn|Ypý Tekó Ybytu Eté|italics=on|nolink=on}} |{{small|({{lang-en|"Our True Essence is the Breath of the Earth"}})}}}}|anthem=|other_name=Six Nations|GDP_PPP=$249.467 billion|GDP_PPP_per_capita=$31,000|GDP_PPP_year=2025|population_census_rank=7th|mapsize=270px}}'''Pindorama''' ({{Langx|tpn|Pindó-rama|4=land of palms}}), also known as the '''Six''' '''Nations''' (''Apatá Abá'') is a [[Communities of Balisca|community]] within the [[Balisca|Baliscan Confederation]] located west of the [[Matarrañya / Cañadapirén]], within the [[Marañón basin]]. It has an area of {{convert|995596.89|km2|sqmi|abbr=on}}, making it the second-largest Baliscan territory. It is also the least-populous community in Balisca, with a population of 7,559,628 in the [[2025 Baliscan census]]. It was known to the Illypno-Mesogeans during the [[W:France Antarctique|colonial years]] as the '''Tava League''', and later as the '''Pindoramí Confederacy''', while the [[Hesperian League|Hesperians]] simply called them the "Five Nations". The peoples of Pindorama included (from east to west) the Jatobá, Guanarú, Itapiranga, Marabá, and Pirajuru. After [[1883 Confederal Convention|1883]], the [[Hesperian League|legation cities]] ([[Maracaju]], [[Araxá]] and [[Sarvaturi]]) were transferred from Hesperian to Pindoramense authority with full citizenship, from which point Pindorama was known as the "Six Nations".  

Notable advancements of pre-colonial Pindoramense indigenous societies included: {{W|terrace farm}}ing, {{W|stonework}}, {{W|wayfinding}} techniques such as the [[W:Celestial navigation|navigation by the stars]], and observations of [[W:Bird migration|migrating birds]], [[W:Swell (ocean)|ocean swells]], and wind patterns, extensive {{W|oral tradition}}, mastery of fishing techniques, finely-woven textiles, herbal medicine, and use of knotted strings for record keeping and communication.

It is organized as a very loose {{W|confederation}} with substantial levels of [[W:One country, two systems#One country, two systems proposals for other countries|indigenous sovereignty alongside that of the legation cities]]. The legation cities operate as [[W:Special administrative region|special administrative regions]], but are under the Pindoramense community's governance. The [[Confederal government of Balisca|confederal government]] provides around $5 billion in {{W|reparations}} annually to the six nations of Pindorama, for distribution to their constituent communes. In response to the {{W|COVID-19 pandemic}}, the confederal government provided (either directly or indirectly), a record $18 billion in support of Pindorama.

